 r←secret MaskSecretHeaders text;LF;lines;b
⍝ `text` is raw HTTP data: lines separated by LF, normally CR LF.
⍝ Returns `text` with the value of every "name: value" line whose name is in `secret` (upper
⍝ case, see `SecretHeaders`) replaced by "***". All other lines are left alone.
 LF←⎕UCS 10
 lines←LF{1↓¨(⍵=⍺)⊂⍵}LF,text                          ⍝ Keeps empty lines, unlike splitting
 b←{':'∊⍵}¨lines
 b[⍸b]←(1 ⎕C{(¯1+⍵⍳':')↑⍵}¨(b/lines)~¨' ')∊secret
 lines[⍸b]←{(⍵↑⍨⍵⍳':'),' ***',(⎕UCS 13)/⍨(⎕UCS 13)=⊃⌽⍵}¨b/lines
 r←1↓∊LF,¨lines
⍝Done
